-- title:
--   Supersingular prolongation with smooth charts, node presentations, Hasse J
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$ and $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. The field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$; $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` is its residue field. Two function fields are involved, both realised as intermediate fields of Laurent series: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, and `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the function field of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ (the kernel of the reduction map furnished by `dvd_sq_mul q M'`); `hle` is the inclusion of the former in the latter, and the element $j$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` always means the image `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. On the residual side, `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` is the subfield of $\kappa$-Laurent series generated by `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`.
--
--   The hypotheses are: a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ with `hW` asserting that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' κ` of places satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace q M'`; a constant reduction `R₀` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` — that is, a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue map onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, together with the scaling axiom and a place map preserving degrees and orders; the compatibility `hR₀`, saying that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image under `coeffMap A.subtype` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its `R₀`-residue is the coefficientwise reduction `coeffMap (residue A) y`; a chosen element $s$ of $W$; and an element $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$.
--
--   Two conditions recur and are named here. Say that $f \in$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is *$j$-regular* if $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at which $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$. Say that a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ *lies over $s$* if for every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` which is $j$-regular and whose `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and every $a \in A$ with `residue A a` equal to the evaluation at $s$ of that `R₀`-residue, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{incl}(f)) - a$ lies in $A$ and in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of a type `FSS`, a field structure and a $\kappa$-algebra structure on it, and a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `FSS` (a valuation subring `R.integers` with surjective residue map onto `FSS` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, plus the scaling axiom), such that the following hold.
--
--   (C1) Some element of `FSS` is transcendental over $\kappa$.
--
--   (C2) For every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` which is $j$-regular and whose `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `R.integers` and its $R$-residue is the image in `FSS` of the evaluation at $s$ of that `R₀`-residue.
--
--   (C3) For every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, the pullback of `R.integers` along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is `R.integers`.
--
--   Moreover there exist a finite set $N$ of places of `FSS` over $\kappa$, a family of subrings $S_Q \subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'`, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_Q : A[X] \to S_Q$ and $\chi_{0,Q} : S_Q \to \kappa$, and sets $D_Q$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, indexed by places $Q$ of `FSS`, with:
--
--   (C4) $|N| = q+1$.
--
--   (C5) (Smooth-point package, for every $Q \notin N$, twelve clauses.) $S_Q$ contains the image of $A$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ for $a \in A$, and $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(C\,a)) =$ `residue A a`, while $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(X)) = 0$; for every $c \in A$ with `residue A c = 0` there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi : S_Q \to A$ with $\chi(\varphi_Q(C\,a)) = a$ for all $a$, with `residue A` $\circ\, \chi = \chi_{0,Q}$, and with $\chi(\varphi_Q(X)) = c$; every $f \in S_Q$ lies in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there is the image of $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$ in the residue field of $Q$; $\varphi_Q(X)$ lies in `R.integers` and its $R$-residue has order $1$ at $Q$; $P \in D_Q$ holds exactly when $P$ is rational (the map from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to the residue field of $P$ is surjective), every $f \in S_Q$ is integral at $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for every $f \in S_Q$ one has $A.\mathrm{valuation}(P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)) < 1$ if and only if $\chi_{0,Q}(f) = 0$; every $\chi : S_Q \to A$ restricting to the identity on $A$ through $\varphi_Q \circ C$ and lifting $\chi_{0,Q}$ is realised by a unique $P \in D_Q$, in the sense that $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) = \chi(f)$ for all $f \in S_Q$; for $P \in D_Q$, an element of `fieldBar q M'` is integral at $P$ precisely when it is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h \in S_Q$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(h) \neq 0$; every non-zero $f$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}(f) = 0$ for all $P \in D_Q$ becomes a unit of $S_Q$ after multiplication by a non-zero constant of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; and every $f \in$ `R.integers` integral at all $P \in D_Q$ lies in $S_Q$.
--
--   (C6) The discs are disjoint: if $Q, Q' \notin N$ and some $P$ lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$, then $Q = Q'$.
--
--   (C7) For $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$, where $j$ is viewed in `fieldBar q M'` through `hle`.
--
--   (C8) (Level equivariance off the nodes.) For every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}($`fieldBar q M'`$)$ generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`: the induced residual automorphism `R.resAut τ` sends $N$ to $N$ and its complement to its complement, and for $Q \notin N$ one has `smulDisc τ` $(D_Q) = D_{\mathrm{R.resAut}\,\tau \,\cdot\, Q}$, where `smulDisc τ D` $= \{P \mid \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in D\}$.
--
--   (C9) (Drinfeld identification.) For every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from `FSS` onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field of the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements $(1,\zeta')$, $\zeta' \in C_s$) such that $\mathrm{card}\,C_s = 2\,\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` — the latter being `jWidthChar q (s.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M'))` divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s` — and such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, with the hypotheses that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves `R.integers` and that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of $(g,\alpha) \mapsto \det(g)\alpha^{q+1}$), conjugating the residual action of `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` by $e$ gives the action of $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ on the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   (C10) (Semilinear transport.) For every semilinear automorphism $g$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (a pair of ring automorphisms of the big field and of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with the structure map) such that `baseAut g` preserves $A$, $g$ preserves `R.integers` and $g$ fixes $j$, for every ring automorphism $\psi$ of $\kappa$ compatible with `baseAut g` on residues, and every ring automorphism $\varphi$ of `FSS` with $R$-residue of $g \cdot f$ equal to $\varphi(R\text{-residue of } f)$: if $Q \notin N$ and $Q'$ is the transport of $Q$ along $\varphi$ (membership in $Q'$ equivalent to membership of $\varphi^{-1}$-image in $Q$), then $Q' \notin N$, $f \in S_Q$ if and only if $g \cdot f \in S_{Q'}$, $\chi_{0,Q'}(g \cdot f) = \psi(\chi_{0,Q}(f))$ for $f \in S_Q$, and $P \in D_Q$ if and only if $g \cdot P \in D_{Q'}$.
--
--   (C11) $N$ is a single orbit: for all $x, x' \in N$ there are $\zeta$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` preserving `R.integers` and $\mathrm{R.resAut}(\zeta,\gamma) \cdot x = x'$.
--
--   (C12) Every $Q \notin N$ is moved: there are $\zeta$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ as above with $\mathrm{R.resAut}(\zeta,\gamma) \cdot Q \neq Q$.
--
--   (C13) (Generators.) There are $n$ and elements $g_0,\dots,g_{n-1}$ of `R.integers` such that each $g_i$ is integral at every $P \in D_Q$ for $Q \notin N$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(g_i) \in A$, and such that every $f \in$ `FSS` integral at all $Q \notin N$ lies in the $\kappa$-subalgebra generated by the $R$-residues of the $g_i$.
--
--   (C14) (Annuli at the nodes.) There is a family of annuli `An x` over $A$ in `fieldBar q M'` (each consisting of a set `dom` of places, a parameter `param`, a modulus in the maximal ideal of $A$, subject to the axioms of `Annulus`: rationality and normalisation of the parameter on `dom`, the bijection of `dom` with admissible moduli values, $\mathrm{ord}(\mathrm{param} - \mathrm{evalAt}\,\mathrm{param}) = 1$, and the unit principle) such that:
--
--   (C14a) for $x \in N$: `(An x).param` lies in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue has order $1$ at $x$, and for every $f \in$ `R.integers` with non-zero $R$-residue and $P.\mathrm{ord}(f) = 0$ for all $P \in$ `(An x).dom`, the quantity $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \cdot P.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{param})^{-x.\mathrm{ord}(R\text{-residue of }f)}$ lies in $A$ and is a unit there, for every such $P$; the modulus of `An x` is non-zero in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; no place of `(An x).dom` lies in any $D_Q$ with $Q \notin N$; and every place of `(An x).dom` lies over $s$ in the sense above;
--
--   (C14b) the domains of `An x`, $x \in N$, are pairwise disjoint;
--
--   (C14c) for $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, preserving `R.integers`, and $x \in N$, `smulDisc τ ((An x).dom)` $=$ `(An (R.resAut τ • x)).dom`;
--
--   (C14d) (Covering.) Every rational place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which lies over $s$ belongs either to some $D_Q$ with $Q \notin N$, or to `(An x).dom` for some $x \in N$;
--
--   (C14e) (Separation.) For distinct $x, x' \in N$ there is $g \in$ `R.integers` with non-zero $R$-residue, with $x.\mathrm{ord}$ of that residue non-zero, with $P.\mathrm{ord}(g) = 0$ for all $P \in$ `(An x).dom`, and such that for every $P \in$ `(An x').dom`, $g$ is integral at $P$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(g)$ is a unit of $A$;
--
--   (C14f) (Node presentations, Hasse $J$, and compatibilities.) There exist: a family of fields `FIx x` with $\kappa$-algebra structures, regular prolongations `Rx x` of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `FIx x`, and places `bx x` of `FIx x` over $\kappa$, indexed by places $x$ of `FSS`; an index type $\Lambda$ with subrings $C'_l \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ all contained in $A$, each a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with elements $\varpi'_l$ and a base index $l_0$; complete discrete valuation rings $W_l$ ($\mathrm{Wc}$), adically complete for their maximal ideals, with elements $\pi_{W,l}$, exponents $E_l \in \mathbb{N}$ and $E_0 \in \mathbb{N}$; sets $S_{nd}$ of places of `fieldBar q M'`, subrings $\mathcal{N}_{nd}$ and $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ of `fieldBar q M'` together with local-ring and Noetherian witnesses, and elements $c_x(nd), c_y(nd), c_u(nd)$ of `fieldBar q M'`; subject to: $\varpi'_l$ generating the elements of $C'_l$ with zero residue in $A$; $C'_{l_0} \le C'_l$ for all $l$; $\varpi'_{l_0} \neq 0$; every element of $A$ algebraic over $C'_{l_0}$; $\pi_{W,l}$ irreducible and $1 \le E_l$; invariance of $\varpi'_{l_0}$ under every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with `A.tameCharacter π τ = 1`; and the existence of $w \ge 1$ and a unit $v$ of $A$ with $(\varpi'_{l_0})^{E_0} = v \pi^w$ in $A$.
--
--   For each $nd \in N$: `bx nd`, $nd$ and all places in $S_{nd}$ are rational; $f \in \mathcal{N}_{nd}$ exactly when $f$ lies in `(Rx nd).integers`, in `R.integers` and in the valuation subring of every $P \in S_{nd}$; elements of $\mathcal{N}_{nd}$ have evaluations in $A$ at all $P \in S_{nd}$; the crossing relation $c_x(nd)\,c_y(nd) = (\varpi'_{l_0})^{E_0} c_u(nd)$ holds; $c_x(nd)$ has zero `Rx nd`-residue and its $R$-residue has order $1$ at $nd$; $c_y(nd)$ has zero $R$-residue and its `Rx nd`-residue has order $1$ at `bx nd` (each such clause conditioned on the relevant integrality); for $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup with trivial tame character, the semilinear automorphism `arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')) τ` stabilises $S_{nd}$ and fixes $c_x(nd)$ and $c_y(nd)$; every element of `fieldBar q M'` is a fraction of elements of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ for some $l$, and also a quotient by an element of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l_0}$ of a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-linear combination of elements of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l_0}$. For each $l$: $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l_0} \le \mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l} \le \mathcal{N}_{nd}$; $P \in S_{nd}$ exactly when $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ is contained in the valuation subring of $P$ and every non-unit of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ evaluates at $P$ into the maximal ideal of $A$; the image of $C'_l$ lies in $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$; every element of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ differs from some element of $C'_l$ by a non-unit; any $C'_l$-linearly independent family of scalars annihilating a combination of elements of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ forces those elements to vanish; there is a subring $B \subseteq \mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ containing $c_x(nd), c_y(nd), c_u(nd)$, with $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ obtained from $B$ by inverting those elements of $B$ that are units of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$, and $B$ generated as a ring by the image of $C'_l$ together with a finite set; $c_x(nd), c_y(nd) \in \mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ and $c_u(nd)$ is a unit there; and there are a ring homomorphism $\sigma$ from $W_l$ to the adic completion of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ at its maximal ideal and a ring isomorphism $\iota$ of that completion with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (πW l ^ E l)` (the ring of two-variable power series over $W_l$ modulo `uvCrossingIdeal`) such that $\sigma(\pi_{W,l})$ is the image of $\varpi'_l$, $\iota \circ \sigma$ is the constant embedding, every element of $C'_l$ is in the image of $\sigma$, and: an element $f$ of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ whose `Rx nd`-residue is non-zero of order $n$ at `bx nd` satisfies $\iota(f) \equiv \gamma V^n$ modulo the ideal generated by the constant $\pi_{W,l}$ and $U$, for some unit $\gamma$ of the crossing model, and symmetrically an $f$ whose $R$-residue is non-zero of order $n$ at $nd$ satisfies $\iota(f) \equiv \gamma U^n$ modulo the ideal generated by the constant $\pi_{W,l}$ and $V$.
--
--   Further, (Hasse $J$) `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` lies in `fieldBar q M'` and there is $a_0 \in A$ such that $J - a_0$ lies in `R.integers` with zero $R$-residue, `residue A a₀`$^q$ equals the evaluation at $s$ of `jGeomGen κ M'`, and there is $c' \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $c'(J - a_0) \in$ `R.integers` of non-zero $R$-residue such that for every $nd \in N$, $J - a_0$ lies in `(Rx nd).integers` with non-zero residue and $nd.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $R$-residue of $c'(J-a_0)$ equals minus the order at `bx nd` of the `Rx nd`-residue of $J - a_0$.
--
--   Finally, in this block: the sets $S_{nd}$, $nd \in N$, are pairwise disjoint; every $P \in S_{nd}$ lies over $s$; for each $\zeta'$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ there is a map $\tau_N$ on places of `FSS` with $\tau_N(nd) \in N$, with `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` carrying $S_{\tau_N(nd)}$ to $S_{nd}$ in the stated equivalence, and with the pullback of `(Rx nd).integers` along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equal to `(Rx (τN nd)).integers`; for $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms preserving `R.integers` and $nd \in N$, `R.resAut τ • nd` lies in $N$ and `smulDisc τ (S nd)` $= S_{\mathrm{R.resAut}\,\tau\,\cdot\,nd}$; $S_{nd} =$ `(An nd).dom` for $nd \in N$; images of elements of `R₀.integers` lie in `(Rx nd).integers`; and for each $nd \in N$ there is a ring homomorphism $j_{nd}$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to `FIx nd` computing the `Rx nd`-residues of images of elements of `R₀.integers` from their `R₀`-residues, and such that an element of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` lies in the valuation subring of $s$ precisely when its image lies in that of `bx nd`.
--
--   (C15) (Drinfeld identification with inertia.) For every ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb{F}_{q^2} \to \kappa$, taken as the algebra structure, and every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, there is a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ with $\mathrm{card}\,C_s = 2\,\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` such that for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` there is a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from `FSS` onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with the two properties: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ (with the integrality hypothesis for `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` and the membership $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1) \in$ `hSubgroup q`), conjugation by $e$ of the residual action of `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` is the action of $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$; and for $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` and a unit $\alpha$ of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ with $\iota(\alpha) =$ `A.tameCharacter π τ`, and $g =$ `arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')) τ`, the automorphism $g$ preserves `R.integers`, and for every ring automorphism $\varphi$ of `FSS` compatible with $g$ through the $R$-residue map, every unit $d$ of $\mathbb{Z}/q$ whose image in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ is $\alpha^{q+1}$ and every membership $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^q)^{-1}, \alpha^q) \in$ `hSubgroup q`, conjugation by $e$ of $\varphi$ is the action of $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^q)^{-1}, \alpha^q)$ on the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   Clauses (C9) and (C15) differ in shape: in (C9) the subgroup $C_s$ and the isomorphism $e$ may depend on $\zeta$ and the algebra structure is quantified as an instance, whereas in (C15) $C_s$ is chosen once for the given embedding $\iota$ and only $e$ depends on $\zeta$, at the price of the additional inertia compatibility.
--
--   This is the structural existence statement for the supersingular part of the semistable model of the full level-$q$ modular curve $X_H(q^2M')$ over a valuation ring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $q$, localised over a supersingular place $s$ of the level-$M'$ curve in characteristic $q$: it produces the regular prolongation, the $q+1$ smooth affine charts with their residue discs, the node annuli with their crossing presentations, the Hasse datum for $J = j(\mathsf{q}^q)$, and the identification of the reduced field with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve, equivariantly for $\Gamma_0(M')$ and for tame inertia. It serves as the single source from which the level-$M'$ covering statements are obtained, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_nodePresentations_crossUnits_inertia`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_nodePresentations_crossUnits_inertia) and by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_tubeAnnuli_width_inertia_discs_charted_inertNodes_nodeRings_nodeCharts_moduliHasse`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_tubeAnnuli_width_inertia_discs_charted_inertNodes_nodeRings_nodeCharts_moduliHasse).
